# Witch Project

Cross-platform game built on **Unity 6** (6000.x). Multiplayer is assumed in all design decisions.

## World

Open, procedurally generated world. Terrain and static layout come from generation (`Game.WorldGeneration`); runtime mutations are tracked separately (see `world-data` rule).

## Architecture at a Glance

| Concern | Mechanism | Location |
|---------|-----------|----------|
| Commands & primitive sync (positions, health, …) | `Game.Server.EventsStream` (bidirectional) | `Assets/Game/Scripts/Server/` |
| Player input | Client-side processing → movement command to server | Never send raw input to server |
| World data (terrain, chunk entities) | Separate storage/patch system | `Assets/Game/Scripts/Storage/` |
| Thread scheduling | `Game.ThreadRules` phases + Unity Jobs/Burst | `Assets/Game/Scripts/ThreadRules.cs` |

Do not conflate EventsStream commands with world-data patches. They serve different purposes and use different transfer paths.

## Code Style

- Match existing conventions in the file being edited (namespaces, `internal` visibility, Burst attributes, unsafe where already used).
- Prefer extending existing types (`ICommand`, `ThreadRules`, `Storage`) over parallel abstractions.
- Minimize main-thread work; push computation to Jobs unless Unity API requires the main thread.
